From 5c45f1b7ac835a19cca7f961e4aa187fe9cc91b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ignaciopd3 <210892957+ignaciopd3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:17:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] Casa: the doorbell card as a column down the right
 third, and openers named gate or door
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The shape chosen in the mockup (option 3): a strip of 320 of 960 dp from top to bottom, the
video, the openers and Close in a list (▲ ▼ or ◀ ▶), and the hint at the bottom. Three text
buttons no longer squeeze into a third of the screen.

Each opener reads "Open the gate" (a button such as Ring Intercom's, or anything whose id or
name says gate, intercom, opener, portal…; a Nuki Opener is a lock) or "Open the door"; two of
one kind on a doorbell go by their Home Assistant names.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
